<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- Revision 2 of the conveyor line: the vendor added a Throughput variable to
     ConveyorType and a second conveyor to the line, and left everything else where it
     was. Same ModelUri as revision 1, so loading this over that one is a reload of the
     same namespace rather than a second model.

     The node ids revision 1 already used mean the same nodes here. That is what lets a
     shadow reload keep a monitored item on ns=N;i=1102 alive across the swap; a node
     id which changed meaning between two revisions would be a modelling error the
     server cannot repair. -->
